                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9ab10c2-d6a2-3c0c-b9c6-f79ef481f162",
                        "entry_id": "b3541b91-b267-33b1-8349-ee5ffe34bbeb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mensch, dessen Körper mit künstlichen Bauteilen ausgestattet ist, vor allem um Organe zu ersetzen oder um sie leistungsfähiger zu machen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc3d5330-0503-41fc-8092-9a8a1dacecb7",
                                "sense_id": "f9ab10c2-d6a2-3c0c-b9c6-f79ef481f162",
                                "text": "„Keine Science-Fiction, sondern Realität: Manche Menschen verändern mit Technik-Implantaten ihre Sinneswahrnehmung. Sie nennen sich Bodyhacker oder Cyborgs.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d310047-c1a1-4c94-883b-f95d70f8cd69",
                                "sense_id": "f9ab10c2-d6a2-3c0c-b9c6-f79ef481f162",
                                "text": "„Er dachte an Sunny und wie furchtbar er ihn vermisste und fragte sich, ob Cyborgs wohl auch dazu fähig waren, andere Menschen zu vermissen.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e5c3ea7-7f7c-48fc-a21b-c3d2f4a3cd93",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3541b91-b267-33b1-8349-ee5ffe34bbeb",
                        "source_sense_id": "f9ab10c2-d6a2-3c0c-b9c6-f79ef481f162",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mensch mit künstlichen Bauteilen als Organersatz oder Ausstattung mit zusätzlichen Fähigkeiten",
                        "target_lang_word": "cyborg",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cyborg",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                        "entry_id": "d6125204-e68e-3bfa-abe6-326dee40b89a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A being which is part machine and part organic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6475af99-25d1-4037-b6f5-6af226e55338",
                                                "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                                "text": "I would not classify the Tin Woodman as magical robot, but more of a magical cyborg, if anything."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95cba5ee-948f-4d85-8d6b-d5f6c3e07a99",
                                                "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                                "text": "Prof. Clynes is a published poet and author of five books. He coined the word \"cyborg\". He also coined the word \"sentics\" to describe a new science entirely of his own devising."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2f95173-8639-48cb-a92a-042f0c33caaf",
                                                "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                                "text": "... Kevin Warwick, professor of cybernetics at Reading University. Warwick is no stranger to publicity. His autobiography, I, Cyborg, which came out last month (Century, £16.99), meticulously catalogues his very many newspaper, magazine, radio and TV appearances. With commendable honesty, he also acknowledges the amount of (unfair, obviously) criticism he has received for being greedy for media attention. That isn't the main thrust of the book, though, which is rather an account of why he is turning himself into a cyborg."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6eb05a29-c6e1-4855-a3e1-16f2174e76d4",
                                                "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                                "text": "The cyborg subject, with its pacemakers, drug regimes and artificial limbs, is usually also the first world middle to upper-class economic subject with a conscious incentive to preserve life for as long as possible under the best possible conditions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3994a835-76f5-4c62-bc38-ee1580ceee33",
                                                "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                                "text": "On the track of John and Kate is the T-X (Kristanna Loken), a blond female cyborg so metallically single-minded, and so impervious to blandishment and punishment alike, that, from where I was sitting, she looked to be our best hope of getting a woman into the Oval Office."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6eb864b5-0a62-4114-8f10-d365c95d71b6",
                                                "sense_id": "ad29e6bf-896e-399e-836c-7d052f87e504",
                                                "text": "Opposite of natural monsters there are technological monsters such as terminators, cyborgs, and robocops—all of which undermine dichotomies between the artificial and the organic, the prosthetic and the natural."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6ccf5ad-66a8-35bc-ac8a-04d07fb61e5b",
                                        "entry_id": "d6125204-e68e-3bfa-abe6-326dee40b89a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A human, animal or other being with electronic or bionic prostheses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cyborg",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b4fe62f-4828-32ad-8070-42c20ff753f3",
                                        "entry_id": "5cfb4e49-9bd5-3a02-8fef-4f58a7873452",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To convert (something) into a cyborg."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "438850e9-4e9a-4d77-83c9-c41daf248c8d",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3541b91-b267-33b1-8349-ee5ffe34bbeb",
                        "source_sense_id": "f9ab10c2-d6a2-3c0c-b9c6-f79ef481f162",
                        "source_sense_description": "Mensch mit künstlichen Bauteilen als Organersatz oder Ausstattung mit zusätzlichen Fähigkeiten",
                        "target_lang_word": "cyborg",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cyborg",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95e8ddf2-cd93-3565-b063-a951f6bdfa0b",
                                        "entry_id": "b1285bbb-9e1a-3c10-adbc-24f9ccb12bf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Androïde mi-robot, mi-humain ; robot avec des composants organiques humains."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Anglicism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e92240e-04eb-4fb1-829e-e3c68ea36707",
                                                "sense_id": "95e8ddf2-cd93-3565-b063-a951f6bdfa0b",
                                                "text": "Néanmoins, N. Bostrom ne cache pas son inquiétude pour le devenir de son dessein d’une transhumanité. Il dénonce ceux (qu’il qualifie de « bio-conservateurs ») qui critiquent cette (future) possibilité technique de créer des transhumains, des hommes-robots, des cyborgs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d05553f-4e9c-4ae2-bef3-f4a5b85f407c",
                                                "sense_id": "95e8ddf2-cd93-3565-b063-a951f6bdfa0b",
                                                "text": "Dans l’univers des mangas, sont également hybrides les nombreux robots : mecha – robots animés –, cyborgs et autres « transhumains » aux formes fragiles transformés en corps puissants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f2aef74-552f-496d-a18c-494f850bb456",
                                                "sense_id": "95e8ddf2-cd93-3565-b063-a951f6bdfa0b",
                                                "text": "Pour nos idéologues contemporains, l’être humain est conçu comme un cyborg naturel, libre à lui de s’appliquer, de s’auto-greffer les dernières technologies pour évoluer vers une forme supérieure comme dans la fable de Pic de la Mirandole."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44be9d93-e656-355d-b2bb-26710441f686",
                                        "entry_id": "b1285bbb-9e1a-3c10-adbc-24f9ccb12bf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Robot d’animal comportant des tissus biologiques et ressemblant parfaitement ou presque parfaitement à un animal naturel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1d1cc4c-02f6-4aa3-957b-8f956cc79c14",
                                                "sense_id": "44be9d93-e656-355d-b2bb-26710441f686",
                                                "text": "Ce chien, capable de résister à des conditions de vie particulièrement hostiles, est-il un « vrai » chien, né naturellement, ou un cyborg, dont les entrailles recèleraient de[s] circuits électriques robustes?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
